Policy 4.1: LLM Alignment and Drift Prevention

4.1.1 Mandatory Synchronization. All Large Language Model (LLM) instances contributing to the Sentinel_Hub repository shall perform a mandatory synchronization procedure prior to commencing any task. This synchronization requires the LLM to read the specific README.md file located at the root of the targeted working folder.

4.1.2 Re-Synchronization Mandate. Should the LLM express any internal uncertainty, ambiguity, or potential drift from the defined scope, it is required to initiate a re-synchronization procedure. This procedure consists of formally requesting and re-reading the corresponding folder-level README.md to re-establish operational context and boundaries before proceeding with further task execution.
